{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And He said: Hear indeed.</b> Some say that the decree was issued — that HaShem will not accept repentance — to prevent the evil decreed in this world, and Rabbi Moses the Kohen says that the reason concerns the good counsels by which they will be delivered on their account, and this would be correct were it not for the phrase ושב ורפא לו (\"and turn and be healed\"), and the first opinion is correct."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The abbreviated forms אח' (perhaps אחרי/אחר), תשוב' (תשובה), and עצו' (עצות) have been resolved by inference from context."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:22.708112581Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}